meta {
  name: add
  type: http
  seq: 8
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/shows/show
  body: formUrlEncoded
  auth: none
}

headers {
  X-BetaSeries-Key: {{apiKey}}
  X-BetaSeries-Version: 3.0
  Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
}

body:form-urlencoded {
  id: 38605
  ~episode_id:
}

docs {
  Add a series to the member's account.

  Backs Client.add_show(). No example block yet: the response has not been
  captured against a real key. The client discards the body (like every other
  write action), so only the error behaviour matters - run this twice on the
  same id to find out what adding an already-followed series returns, and
  narrow it in const.py/exceptions.py if it turns out to have its own code
  (today it lands in the generic Error/HomeAssistantError path).
}
